Yoothika Patel, CSE Dept. 
6External JavaScript Advantages 
▪Placing scripts in external files has some advantages: 
•It separates HTML and code 
•It makes HTML and JavaScript easier to read and maintain 
•Cached JavaScript files can speed up page loads 
•It helps in reusability of code in more than one HTML file. 
•It enables both web designer and coder to work with html 
and js files parallelly and separately. 
•Length of the code reduce as only we need to specify the 
location of the js file. 


--- Page 7 ---
07-02-2026 
Yoothika Patel, CSE Dept. 
7Disadvantage of External JavaScript 
▪The stealer may download the coder’s code using url of the js file 
▪The two js files are dependent on one another then failure in one 
file may affect the execution of the other dependent file. 
▪A tiny to large change in the js code cause unexpected  results in 
all its dependent files. 
▪We need to check each file that depend on commonly created 
external javascript file. 
▪If it is few lines of code ,then better to implement the internal 
javascript code. 


