41JavaScript Array Operations 
1.Concatenation - merges arrays. 
2.Sorting- arranges numbers correctly using a function. 
If a-b is negative  (a<b) , a  is placed before b. 
If a-b is positive  (a>b), b is placed before a. 
If a-b is zero ,their position remain unchanged. 
3.Reversing- flips the order. 
4.Splice- removes and inserts elements. 
array.splice(startIndex, deleteCount, item1, item2, ...); 
5.Slice- extracts part of an array. 
        array.slice(startIndex, endIndex); 


