47Forms using DOM 
▪We can access the elements of form in DOM quite easily using the 
name/id of the form. 
▪Example : 
HTML 
<html> 
    <body> 
      <form name=“myForm”> 
        <input type=“text” name=“uname”> 
        <input type=“text” name=“pword”> 
        <input type=“button” onClick=“f()”> 
     </form> 
    </body> 
</html> JS
function f() 
{
   var a = document.forms[“myForm”]; 
   var u = a.uname.value; 
   var p = a.pword.value; 
   if(u==“admin” && p==“123”) 
   {
      alert(“valid”); 
   }
   else 
   {
       alert(“Invalid”); 
   }
}

